# SDL3 is taken from the Odin installation by copy_sdl.bat / copy_sdl.sh rather
# than kept here. A committed copy goes stale without saying so -- this repo
# carried SDL 3.3.0 while vendor:sdl3's bindings were generated against 3.4.2.
SDL3.dll
libSDL3.so

# Android. Everything under matchbox/android/libs is fetched or cross-compiled
# by matchbox/android_sdl.bat and matchbox/android.bat, so none of it is
# committed -- same reasoning as SDL3.dll above, and libSDL3.so is already
# covered by the rule at the top. They live inside matchbox so that dropping the
# folder into a project brings its Android support with it.
matchbox/android/libs/*.a
matchbox/android/libs/SDL3-classes.jar

# Build output, and the self-signed debug key android_apk.bat makes on demand.
# The key is regenerated if missing; a lost one only means the next install has
# to be an uninstall first, since Android will not replace an apk signed by a
# different key.
build/
matchbox/android/debug.keystore
*.apk
